      "caption": {
        "known": true,
        "value": "White flower that blooms in catacombs.\nEach a soundless bell used to summon spirits.\n\nStrengthens ashes to +9.\n\nSpirit tuning is not merely the simple act of imbuing strength. It is an art that lies somewhere between tuning an instrument and conducting a conversation, leaving both parties enriched.",
        "provenance": {
          "source": "legacy_db_data",
          "method": "copied from legacy ItemTexts.Caption"
        }
      },
      "description": {
        "known": true,
        "value": "Strengthen ashes to +9",
        "provenance": {
          "source": "legacy_db_data",
          "method": "copied from legacy ItemTexts.Description"
        }
      },
      "location": {
        "known": true,
        "value": "Leyndell Catacombs : There are two in this dungeon, which is accessed from below the Subterranean Shunning-Grounds . One is to the right, just before the first flame statue. The second is at the back of the third floor of this intentionally confusing dungeon, which involves three similar copies of the same floor. Please see the Leyndell Catacombs page for a detailed description of how to get through it to find the second Grave Glovewort [9].; Six can be found within Consecrated Snowfield Catacombs in Consecrated Snowfield . First is found in a room filled with imps. Another one is found in the room before taking the stairs to the second floor of the frost trap. Third is on second floor by the trap. A fourth is guarded by two Cleanrot Knights in a room in the second floor by the trap. A fifth one can be looted on the third floor by the lever to open the boss door. Final one is in a room in the second floor, guarded by a Burial Tree Watchdog. [ Map Link ]; One is found behind the first Lesser Burial Watchdog encountered, in a room under the circle of light.",
        "provenance": {
          "source": "legacy_db_data",
          "method": "copied from legacy ItemTexts.Location"
        }
      },
